---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of Service — Schedule | shiv.rocks" description="Terms of Service for Schedule, a workforce scheduling and team management application.">
  <Header />
  <main class="pt-32 pb-20 px-6">
    <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">

      <div class="mb-12">
        <a href="/schedule" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-mono text-text-muted hover:text-text-primary transition-colors duration-300 mb-8">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M10.5 19.5 3 12m0 0 7.5-7.5M3 12h18" />
          </svg>
          Back to Schedule
        </a>
        <h1 class="font-heading font-bold text-4xl md:text-5xl mb-3">Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="text-text-muted font-mono text-sm">Effective Date: March 7, 2026</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-content space-y-8 text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        <p>Welcome to Schedule. By using our application, you agree to these Terms of Service ("Terms"). Please read them carefully.</p>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-heading font-bold text-xl text-text-primary mb-3">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
          <p>By creating an account or using Schedule, you agree to be bound by these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the application.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-heading font-bold text-xl text-text-primary mb-3">2. Description of Service</h2>
          <p>Schedule is a workforce scheduling and team management application that allows users to create teams, assign tasks, manage schedules, and collaborate with team members.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-heading font-bold text-xl text-text-primary mb-3">3. Account Registration</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 ml-2">
            <li>You must provide accurate and complete information when creating an account.</li>
            <li>You are responsible for maintaining the security of your account credentials.</li>
            <li>You must be at least 13 years old to use Schedule.</li>
            <li>One person may not maintain more than one account.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-heading font-bold text-xl text-text-primary mb-3">4. Acceptable Use</h2>
          <p>You agree not to:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 ml-2 mt-2">
            <li>Use the service for any unlawful purpose.</li>
            <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to other users' accounts or data.</li>
            <li>Interfere with or disrupt the service or its infrastructure.</li>
            <li>Upload malicious content or spam.</li>
            <li>Impersonate another person or entity.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-heading font-bold text-xl text-text-primary mb-3">5. User Content</h2>
          <p>You retain ownership of content you create (team names, task descriptions, messages). By using Schedule, you grant us a limited license to store and display your content to authorized team members as part of the service's functionality.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-heading font-bold text-xl text-text-primary mb-3">6. Team Administration</h2>
          <p>Team administrators are responsible for managing their team's membership, tasks, and content. Administrators may remove members and delete team content at their discretion.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-heading font-bold text-xl text-text-primary mb-3">7. Account Deletion</h2>
          <p>You may delete your account at any time from the Settings screen. Upon deletion, your user profile and authentication credentials will be permanently removed. Team data and tasks you contributed may remain visible to other team members.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-heading font-bold text-xl text-text-primary mb-3">8. Service Availability</h2>
          <p>We strive to maintain reliable service but do not guarantee uninterrupted availability. We may modify, suspend, or discontinue any part of the service at any time with reasonable notice.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-heading font-bold text-xl text-text-primary mb-3">9. Limitation of Liability</h2>
          <p>Schedule is provided "as is" without warranties of any kind. To the maximum extent permitted by law, we shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, or consequential damages arising from your use of the service.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-heading font-bold text-xl text-text-primary mb-3">10. Indemnification</h2>
          <p>You agree to indemnify and hold harmless Schedule and its operators from any claims, damages, or expenses arising from your use of the service or violation of these Terms.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-heading font-bold text-xl text-text-primary mb-3">11. Changes to Terms</h2>
          <p>We may update these Terms from time to time. Continued use of Schedule after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated Terms.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-heading font-bold text-xl text-text-primary mb-3">12. Governing Law</h2>
          <p>These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of California, United States, without regard to conflict of law provisions.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-heading font-bold text-xl text-text-primary mb-3">13. Contact</h2>
          <p>For questions about these Terms, contact us at: <a href="mailto:legal@shiv.rocks" class="text-accent-2 hover:text-accent-3 transition-colors">legal@shiv.rocks</a></p>
        </section>
      </div>

    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
